<title>RUSSIA: TABLE-Russia to auction bills, bonds on July 23.</title>
<headline>TABLE-Russia to auction bills, bonds on July 23.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-07-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Russian Finance Ministry will auction 9.00 trillion roubles of 364-day GKO discount Treasury bills (series 21080) and 8.00 trillion roubles of 728-day bonds (series 24016) on July 23, the Central Bank said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>    Series number		   21080</p>
<p>    Issue volume		    9.00 trln rbls</p>
<p>    Denomination		    1.00 million</p>
<p>    Tenor			     364 days</p>
<p>    Maturity date		   July 22, 1998</p>
<p>    Series number		   24016</p>
<p>    Issue volume		    8.00 trln rbls</p>
<p>    Denomination		    1.00 million</p>
<p>    Tenor			     728 days</p>
<p>    Maturity date		   July 21, 1999</p>
<p>    First coupon date	     January 21, 1998</p>
<p>    First coupon		    17.42 pct annual</p>
<p>First coupon (money terms)  86,861 roubles</p>
<p>The bond will pay semi-annual interest for 182-day periods, with coupon dates on January 21, 1998; July 22, 1998; January 20, 1999; July 21, 1999.</p>
<p>On July 23 the Finance Ministry will also repay 6.45 trillion roubles in a maturing issue of 210-day T-bills (series 22064).</p>
<p>It will also pay 237.83 billion roubles in interest on the two-year OFZ interest-bearing government bond (series 24009) maturing October 1998.</p>
<p>--Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
